message.content:
You are fixing one performance problem in inkling, an Electron + React + TypeScript + Vite app with node:sqlite in the main process (Bun 1.4.2). Read AGENTS.md at the worktree root first. Its rules apply.

WORKSPACE: C:\Users\chris\.t3\worktrees\inkling\perf-library-io (branch perf/library-io). Work ONLY there. Never touch any other worktree or the live library. Three other agents are editing this same worktree right now:
- one on capture IPC and background thumbnails;
- one on video posters;
- one on the Settings Archive tab.
Make targeted edits with the Edit tool only. Never rewrite a shared file with Write, especially electron/main.mjs, which others are also editing. If an edit fails because the text moved, re-read and retry. Run NO git commands that change state (no add, commit, checkout, stash, reset or restore). The maintainer commits. Do not launch dev servers or Electron.

TASK: the custom asset protocol handler in electron/main.mjs (around line 325, `const body = request.method === "HEAD" ? null : await readFile(realFile);`) reads the whole file into memory for every request. It also has no Range support, so a large local video or PDF is read fully before a byte is served, and video seeking can't work properly.
- Stream the file instead (fs.createReadStream turned into a web stream via Readable.toWeb, or whatever works with Electron's protocol.handle Response).
- Support single byte-range requests: 206 with Content-Range, and 416 with `Content-Range: bytes */size` for unsatisfiable ranges. Send Accept-Ranges: bytes and Content-Length. Keep HEAD working.
- Keep every existing security check exactly as strict: realpath containment inside the assets directory, method checks and content types.
- Caching: find out whether asset paths are immutable. Thumbnails may be regenerated at the same path. Only add cache headers that are correct and actually help for a custom protocol in Electron (ETag/Last-Modified from stat, for example). Don't add headers that do nothing, and say what you chose and why.
- Move the request-to-response logic into a small module (e.g. electron/asset-response.mjs) so it can be tested without Electron, and keep main.mjs wiring thin.

TESTS: add focused bun tests covering:
- a full GET with the streamed body;
- HEAD;
- valid ranges, including open-ended `bytes=100-` and suffix `bytes=-100`;
- an unsatisfiable range giving 416;
- a malformed range giving a full 200;
- path escape and symlink containment still rejected.
Run `bun test <your test file>`, `bunx biome check <changed files>`, and `bun run typecheck`. Check the exit code with `echo $?`, not through a pipe. If typecheck errors are only in files another agent is editing, say so instead of fixing them.

Code style: match the surrounding code. Comments only say why. No new dependencies.

REPORT (under 200 words): files changed, the response behavior, the caching decision and why, tests run with results, and anything left unfinished.

